  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual accusation",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto a specific visual or textual element via deictic pronouns like 'me', 'you', or 'your'. However, the meme's structure inherently projects the user's perspective onto the textual material ('has more skeletons in her closet than jeffrey dahmer') and the visual material (Hillary_Clinton) as the target of the accusation. The user is implicitly positioned as the one interpreting or endorsing the hateful comparison, thereby projecting their own stance onto the scene. The projection is onto the textual material which makes the accusation, and the visual material which embodies the target of that accusation.",
